  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Danone is a leading global food and beverage company based in Paris, operating in over 120 countries with a focus on health-focused products. Its core business lines include Essential Dairy and Plant-Based Products (e.g., Activia, Silk), Waters (e.g., Evian), and Specialized Nutrition (e.g., Aptamil, Danone Research & Innovation). Founded in 1919, the company emphasizes sustainability, aiming to \"bring health through food to as many people as possible\". Key aspects of Danone include: Product Portfolio: A wide range of dairy, plant-based, water, and specialized nutrition products, with popular brands including Activia, Danimals, Evian, Oikos, and Silk. Sustainability & Purpose: As a Certified B Corporation, Danone is committed to regenerative agriculture, reducing methane emissions, and protecting water resources. Innovation: Danone Research & Innovation utilizes AI and data to focus on gut health, microbiome science, and personalized nutrition. Market Position: Listed on Euronext Paris, it is a major player in the global food industry with a strong emphasis on health-conscious consumers. Recent Developments: In 2026, the company was noted for acquiring meal-replacement firm Huel to expand its nutritional portfolio and experienced voluntary recalls of infant formula in Germany due to ingredient issues.",
